# tokensave local index - rebuildable cache, not shared state.
.tokensave/

# graphify knowledge-graph output - a rebuildable local artifact, not shared state.
# CORRECTED 2026-09-20: the previous comment here said the graph "cannot be refreshed
# in place" because manifest.json carries no root key. That was wrong twice over - the
# root lives in graphify-out/.graphify_root, not the manifest, and it held a Git Bash
# path that native Windows Python resolved to a real but code-free shadow directory, so
# graphify honestly reported "No code files found". Fixed in one line; `graphify update`
# refreshes it fine now. Still ignored because it is a local cache, not because it is dead.
graphify-out/

# Orchestration scratch under .claude/tasks/. The three files that ARE tracked there -
# whattask.json, runs.jsonl, decisions.jsonl - are the durable record and stay tracked.
# These two are neither durable nor shared:
#   serial.lock   the lock holder registry, machine-local and pid-bearing. It holds "[]"
#                 when idle, so it always exists and always differs between machines.
#   interview.json  /runhuman's research cache. It holds questions it is ABOUT to ask,
#                 never answers - answers go to decisions.jsonl - so it is safe to
#                 delete at any time, at the cost of redoing the research.
.claude/tasks/serial.lock
.claude/tasks/serial.lock.d/
.claude/tasks/interview.json
